,"person_slug":"tanya-plibersek","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tom French","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11039","person_slug":"tom-french","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Burke","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10081","person_slug":"tony-burke","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tracey Roberts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10994","person_slug":"tracey-roberts","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Trish Cook","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11037","person_slug":"trish-cook","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zaneta Mascarenhas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10999","person_slug":"zaneta-mascarenhas","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zhi Soon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11049","person_slug":"zhi-soon","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Business — Rearrangement","noes":13,"question":"Andrew Gee I move: That so much of the standing and sessional orders be suspended as would prevent the following from occurring immediately: (1) the AI Kill Switch and Data Centre Control Bill 2026 being called on; (2) debate on the second reading of the bill proceeding immediately for a period of no longer than one hour; and (3) any questions required to complete passage of the bill then being put without delay. The standing orders must be suspended immediately, because artificial intelligence poses a direct threat to the future of humanity. We must not rush headlong into a technology that we don't even know we can control. Currently, humanity is standing in the middle of an uncontrolled technological race, and the very people building these systems are begging us for the brakes to be applied. In just the past week, the public facade of the AI industry has cracked. One Anthropic employee recently publicly stated: … we really do earnestly believe AI could kill all humans! I personally think it is \\>10% within the next decade. Basically, it's an admission that the industry does not yet have a plan to control superintelligent AI. Another Anthropic researcher who recently resigned warned that corporate labs 'are racing straight to self-improving superintelligence and gambling with our lives'. Another Anthropic AI safety researcher quit, stating: The world is in peril. And not just from AI, or bioweapons, but from a whole series of interconnected crises unfolding in this very moment. They were his words. Now Jack Clark, one of the founders of Anthropic, has publicly stated that we need a mandatory 'kill switch' and that it needs to be checked by third parties. These are the people who created this technology. They are telling us that they need help with putting the brakes on and bringing it under control. In developing AI, the profits of billionaires and tech corporations must not be put ahead of our communities, our country or the future of humanity itself. Anthropic C","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-10781","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2026-09-16/1"}
